opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Typed transport-independent CometBFT and Cosmos gRPC client"
description: """
The CometBFT JSON-RPC method catalogue, the SDK query and tx services, gas
and fee estimation, a tagged confirmation state and the submission state
machine -- all pure. The transport is a module type.

Confirmation is tagged, not boolean. A code-0 broadcast_tx_sync means the
transaction entered a mempool; delivery is a tx query returning code 0 at a
height, and finality is depth beyond that. Conflating the three is the
commonest way to report a failed transfer as a successful one."""
